  "_comment": "Prize draws at the till (issue #138 phase 1). A set is bought whole (set_cost_yen, booked as an ORDER) and sold one ticket at a time for ticket_price_yen over days days; every ticket wins one prize of the set, drawn without replacement from an order shuffled when the set is bought (seeded by the command id, kept in the save, so a loaded game never draws again); the last ticket also gets the last_one prize. A customer at the till buys a ticket with buy_rate x hype (hype_start falling to hype_end over the days, x top_bonus while the top prize is left), a second one with second_rate, within the cash left; a set keeps a few more people coming while its top prize is left (visitors). Unsold tickets at the end are written off (WASTAGE at their share of the set cost). Fictional mascots and goods only; no real brand, character or draw name; in-game money only. Initial values, to be tuned by play.",
